{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>You broke</b> — doubled by the disappearing of the ayin, like פור התפוררה, or like ויפרפרני; the opposite of it. The meaning: for Your dominion rules over earth, as He mentioned, בקרב הארץ — in the sea — and the taninim that are in it. And some say: for this hints at the splitting of the Sea of Reeds." "<b>And the meaning of You shattered</b> — its reversal is 'to shatter.' And some say: for the taninim are Pharaoh and his officers."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 74, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:28.643239238Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}